## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F3 | open | BLOCKING | CHANGELOG.md | 🚨 blocking the merge commit s changelog resolution deletes main s gh 2394 and gh 2404 unreleased entries merging origin main into this branch 0547ef5a51 — merge origin main into ai gh 2408 resolved the changelog conflict by keeping the branch side byte identical git diff 8e74c74dd4 0547ef5a51 changelog md is empty since the merge base is now main s tip 9673f87298 the pr diff itself removes the entries main added feat 2394 compaction 2 0 v2 1 … 12 lines main s changelog 16 fix 2404 load drop retry test — bsd time branch … 3 lines main s changelog 31 git diff origin main head changelog md → 13 24 13 14 15 lines of main s entries deleted the 8 line gh 2408 entry added on top on merge ours base for this file main s unreleased silently loses both entries why it matters changelog md is curated only — new lines go under unreleased and the release folds them into the tag s section at publish staging time file header gh 1522 agents md § commits and releases if this pr merges before the next release cut the v1 0 776 release notes permanently lose the compaction 2 0 v2 1 and gh 2404 entries — and no gate catches it content is not measured the full suite passes green with the deletion in place this is also out of scope a gh 2408 ci fix must not touch the gh 2394 gh 2404 entries at all fix redo the merge resolution for this one file — take main s changelog verbatim and re insert the gh 2408 entry at the top of unreleased bash git checkout origin main changelog md then re add the 8 line fix ci gh 2408 … block directly under unreleased nothing else in the merge lost content the full pr delta is 4 files only changelog md carries deletions |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

